🚀 **Project Highlight: Emotion Detection from Text using Deep Learning**

I’m excited to share my latest **NLP & Deep Learning project — Emotion Detection from Text**, where I developed a deep learning model to identify emotions expressed in text.

🎯 **Project Objective**
The goal was to move beyond simple positive/negative sentiment classification and automatically identify **6 emotions: Anger, Fear, Joy, Love, Sadness, and Surprise**.

🔍 **Approach & Key Steps**
• Cleaned and normalized text using Regular Expressions
• Removed URLs, mentions, special characters, and duplicate text
• Applied tokenization and sequence padding
• Encoded emotion labels using Label Encoding
• Built a deep learning architecture using **Embedding + GRU layers + Dropout + Softmax**
• Used Early Stopping and validation during training
• Evaluated performance using Accuracy, ROC-AUC, Confusion Matrix, and Classification Report

📊 **Model Performance**
✅ Test Accuracy: **93.10%**
✅ Test ROC-AUC: **0.9971**
✅ Weighted F1-Score: **0.93**

💡 **Project Impact**
This project demonstrates how NLP and deep learning can transform unstructured text into actionable emotional insights. A solution like this can support **customer feedback analysis, social media monitoring, product review analysis, and understanding user opinions at scale**, helping organizations make more data-driven decisions.

🧠 **What I Learned**
This project strengthened my practical skills in **NLP preprocessing, sequence modeling, GRU architecture, multi-class classification, model evaluation, and deep learning workflows**.

🛠️ **Tech Stack:**
Python | Pandas | NumPy | Scikit-learn | TensorFlow | Keras | NLP | Deep Learning

I’m open to opportunities in **Data Science | Machine Learning | NLP | AI**.

